# Phase Roadmap Hygiene

Use phase docs as pickup/navigation pages only. Tickets in `docs/Roadmap/tickets/CS-*.md` remain authoritative for scope, dependencies, acceptance criteria, and status.

When a phase is completed, a ready set changes, or the team agrees on a roadmap adjustment:

- Update affected tickets first. Follow `ticket-status-hygiene.mdc` for `status`, `depends_on`, and acceptance criteria. Sync the owning `docs/Roadmap/EPIC-*.md` Definition of done bullets and epic `status` via `epic-status-hygiene.mdc`.
- Keep phase-local `Ready Now` sections limited to tickets that are actually unblocked and ready according to ticket frontmatter.
- Sync the global `Current Ready Picks` lists in `docs/Roadmap/phases/README.md` and `docs/Roadmap/PARALLEL_WORK_PLAN.md` in the same change when current picks or lane guidance changes.
- Preserve the phase-first lane vocabulary: `FE WORK`, `BE WORK`, `INFRA WORK`, and `API / AI CONNECTIONS`.
- Bump `last_updated` on edited roadmap, phase, or plan docs.
- If phase order or epic mapping changes, update `docs/Roadmap/README.md` and include the dependency rationale. Follow `parallel-roadmap-work.mdc`.
- Link to PRDs, domain docs, analysis docs, and ADRs instead of copying requirements into phase docs.
- Keep project verification optional; never make it a blocker for contract upload, analysis, report generation, or delivery.
